        "heading": "1. What is HTML Basic Structure & Boilerplate?",
        "content": "### What is this?\nEvery HTML document follows a strict parent-child hierarchy. The DOCTYPE informs the browser of the version, html wraps everything, head stores instructions, and body holds visible items.\n\n### Key Features & Benefits\n- **DOCTYPE**: DOCTYPE html ensures the browser renders in modern Standards Mode instead of Quirks Mode.\n- **lang=\"en\"**: lang=\"en\" declares the human language for screen readers and search engines.\n- **meta**: meta charset=\"UTF-8\" ensures all international characters, accents, and symbols display correctly.\n- **meta**: meta name=\"viewport\" ensures responsive scaling on smartphones and tablets.",
