        "content": "### What is this?\nThe <head> element is a container for metadata (data about data) and is placed between the <html> tag and the <body> tag. Metadata is not displayed to the user.\n\n### Key Features & Benefits\n- **<title>**: <title> sets the name of the tab and Google search snippet headline.\n- **<meta**: <meta charset=\"UTF-8\"> declares universal character encoding.\n- **<meta**: <meta name=\"viewport\"> enables mobile responsiveness.\n- **<meta**: <meta name=\"description\"> provides the 160-character summary for Google search results.\n- **<link>**: <link> connects external stylesheets, fonts, and favicons.\n- **<base>**: <base> specifies a base URL for all relative links in the document.",
