        "detailedAnswer": "The <head> element is a container for metadata (data about data) and is placed between the <html> tag and the <body> tag. Metadata is not displayed to the user.\n\nKey advantages include:\n- <title> sets the name of the tab and Google search snippet headline.\n- <meta charset=\"UTF-8\"> declares universal character encoding.\n- <meta name=\"viewport\"> enables mobile responsiveness.\n\nUsing this standard element ensures browser compatibility, accessibility for screen readers, and search engine optimization.",
