        "heading": "1. What is HTML Entities?",
        "content": "### What is this?\nSome characters are reserved in HTML. For example, if you write < or > the browser thinks it is an HTML tag. To display these characters literally, you must use HTML entities.\n\n### Key Features & Benefits\n- **Entity**: Entity Name: Starts with & and ends with ; (e.g. &lt; for less than <).\n- **Entity**: Entity Number: Numerical code (e.g. &#60;).\n- **&lt;**: &lt; displays < (less than)\n- **&gt;**: &gt; displays > (greater than)\n- **&amp;**: &amp; displays & (ampersand)\n- **&quot;**: &quot; displays \" (double quote)\n- **&copy;**: &copy; displays © (copyright)\n- **&nbsp;**: &nbsp; inserts a non-breaking space (prevents words from splitting onto a new line).",
