    "overview": "### What is this topic about?\n**HTML Symbols & Emojis: UTF-8 Special Characters** is a core part of the **HTML & Semantic Web** track.\n\nWith modern UTF-8 encoding, HTML can natively display thousands of mathematical symbols, currency symbols, arrows, and colored emojis.\n\n### Why Learn This?\n- Ensure <meta charset=\"UTF-8\"> is present in your <head> so emojis display correctly.\n- Math symbols: &plusmn; (±), &infin; (∞), &sum; (∑), &radic; (√).\n- Currency: &euro; (€), &pound; (£), &yen; (¥), &#8377; (₹).\n- Arrows: &larr; (←), &rarr; (→), &uarr; (↑), &darr; (↓).\n- Emojis are just characters! You can copy/paste emojis directly or use decimal codes (&#128640; for 🚀).",
