    "overview": "### What is this topic about?\n**HTML Audio: The <audio> Element & Sound Playback** is a core part of the **HTML & Semantic Web** track.\n\nThe <audio> element is used to play sound content natively on a web page, such as background music, podcasts, or sound notifications.\n\n### Why Learn This?\n- controls displays the native audio play/pause bar and volume slider.\n- Supported formats: MP3 (universal support), WAV (lossless), and OGG (open source).\n- autoplay starts audio automatically (subject to browser sound policies).\n- loop repeats the audio continuously when it finishes.",
