        "content": "### What is this?\nThe <link> element is an official HTML element belonging to the Document metadata category. Specifies relationships between the current document and an external resource. This element is most commonly used to link to CSS but is also used to establish site icons (both \"favicon\" style icons and icons for the home screen and apps on mobile devices) among other things.\n\n### Key Features & Benefits\n- **Part**: Part of the official WHATWG HTML Living Standard and MDN specification.\n- **Categorized**: Categorized under Document metadata.\n- **Semantic**: Semantic element mapped directly into the browser DOM and Accessibility Tree.\n- **Fully**: Fully supported across all modern web browsers (Chrome, Edge, Safari, Firefox).",
