        "id": "what-is-and-features",
        "heading": "1. What is The <i> Element?",
        "content": "### What is this?\nThe <i> element is an official HTML element belonging to the Inline text semantics category. Represents a range of text that is set off from the normal text for some reason, such as idiomatic text, technical terms, and taxonomical designations, among others. Historically, these have been presented using italicized type, which is the original source of the &lt;i&gt; naming of this element.\n\n### Key Features & Benefits\n- **Part**: Part of the official WHATWG HTML Living Standard and MDN specification.\n- **Categorized**: Categorized under Inline text semantics.\n- **Semantic**: Semantic element mapped directly into the browser DOM and Accessibility Tree.\n- **Fully**: Fully supported across all modern web browsers (Chrome, Edge, Safari, Firefox).",
